{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And you shall not wrong one another.</b> Here He warned against verbal wrong — that one must not needle his fellow, nor give him counsel that is not fit for him, suited to the adviser's own path and benefit. And if you say: Who knows whether I intended harm? Therefore it says וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּאֱלֹהֶיךָ — the One who knows thoughts, He knows. For any matter handed over to the heart, which none recognizes except the one whose thought is in his heart, concerning it Scripture says וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּאֱלֹהֶיךָ (Sifra; Bava Metzia 58)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:18.121853410Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}